From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] d3d11: a keyed mutex's release carries the work queued before it

What a device did to a shared texture before IDXGIKeyedMutex::ReleaseSync is
what the next owner sees, on Windows. DXVK waited only for work already
submitted against the image: a clear still queued in the context, or
deferred by DxvkContext and not flushed at submission because the image was
still in its default layout, ran after the release, so the other process
read the previous contents. Chromium (and Qt WebEngine, in Sigil) share
each frame from their GPU process under a keyed mutex; on real GPUs the
second process saw stale or empty frames. ReleaseSync now flushes the
context before waiting, and a submission flushes the deferred clears of
every shared image, not only those of images out of their default layout.

---
diff --git a/src/d3d11/d3d11_resource.cpp b/src/d3d11/d3d11_resource.cpp
index ef7b058..cef720d 100644
--- a/src/d3d11/d3d11_resource.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d11/d3d11_resource.cpp
@@ -122,6 +122,14 @@ namespace dxvk {
       if (!multithread.GetMultithreadProtected() && !std::exchange(s_errorShown, true))
         Logger::warn("D3D11DXGIKeyedMutex::ReleaseSync: Called without context locking enabled.");
 
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_RELEASESYNC_NO_FLUSH
+      /* Stained Glass OS (dxvk/patches/0004): what the context did to the resource before
+       * ReleaseSync is what the next owner sees, as on Windows. A clear (or other work) still
+       * queued in the context did not make the image busy, so the wait below returned at once
+       * and the other process read the old contents -- Chromium's and Qt WebEngine's frames,
+       * shared from their GPU process, stood still. Submit it first; the wait then covers it. */
+      context->Flush();
+#endif
       D3D10DeviceLock lock = context->LockContext();
       context->WaitForResource(*texture->GetImage(), DxvkCsThread::SynchronizeAll, D3D11_MAP_READ_WRITE, 0);
     }
diff --git a/src/dxvk/dxvk_context.cpp b/src/dxvk/dxvk_context.cpp
index 7c6a4c8..8742c86 100644
--- a/src/dxvk/dxvk_context.cpp
+++ b/src/dxvk/dxvk_context.cpp
@@ -9706,9 +9706,27 @@ namespace dxvk {
 
     for (const auto& image : m_nonDefaultLayoutImages) {
       if (image->info().shared)
-        hasSharedClear = flushDeferredClear(*image, image->getAvailableSubresources());
+        hasSharedClear |= flushDeferredClear(*image, image->getAvailableSubresources());
     }
 
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_SHARED_CLEAR_STAYS_DEFERRED
+    /* Stained Glass OS (dxvk/patches/0004): a shared image cleared while still in its default
+     * layout is not among the images above, so its clear stayed deferred past the submission
+     * and another process opening the image never saw it (Chromium/Qt WebEngine frames shared
+     * under a keyed mutex stood still on real GPUs). Flush every shared image's clears. */
+    std::vector<const DxvkImage*> sharedCleared;
+
+    for (const auto& entry : m_deferredClears) {
+      const DxvkImage* image = entry.imageView->image();
+
+      if (image->info().shared && std::find(sharedCleared.begin(), sharedCleared.end(), image) == sharedCleared.end())
+        sharedCleared.push_back(image);
+    }
+
+    for (const DxvkImage* image : sharedCleared)
+      hasSharedClear |= flushDeferredClear(*image, image->getAvailableSubresources());
+#endif
+
     if (hasSharedClear)
       flushBarriers();
 
